// Deadlock-watchdog runtime hooks (bindings to compiler-emitted C).
// 
// The compiler emits real implementations when the program uses `fork`,
// feeding the scheduler's blocked-task counter so a watchdog thread can
// detect a global stall, and no-op stubs otherwise. Only exercised when
// FUN_DEADLOCK_WATCHDOG_MS arms the watchdog.

// Mark the current thread as entering a blocking channel wait.
pub fun __fun_wd_enter_wait();

// Mark the current thread as leaving a blocking channel wait (records progress).
pub fun __fun_wd_leave_wait();

// Prints a "possible deadlock" diagnostic to stderr: `blocked_or_count` is
// the blocked task count (scheduler) or channel occupancy,
// `pending_or_cap` is pending tasks (scheduler) or channel capacity, and
// `stall_ms` is how long no progress has been observed.
pub fun __fun_wd_warn(num blocked_or_count, num pending_or_cap, num stall_ms);
